{
  "_help": [
    "The days of the people aboard this ship. Restart the game after changing this file. A file here turns on the living clock for the place it's named after.",
    "spots are places on the levels: [level, column, row], with \"left\" at the end if the person's name should go to the left of them. A spot can be on a bunk or a bench. Columns and rows count from 0 at the top left of the level's plan.",
    "groups are lists of spots for many people, like a mess bench. Each person takes the next one that's free. A group entry with from and to fills a whole row, every step squares.",
    "Each person's day is a list of what they start doing, and when: they leave for it at that time, give or take a few minutes, and it lasts until the next one. It wraps around at midnight.",
    "go is where they go: post means their usual place in the map's file, or it's the name of a spot or a group. @bridge means anywhere on that level, wherever's free, and >bridge means out by one of that level's doors. pick is a list of those, and they choose one each day. rounds is a list they walk around, a stop every few minutes.",
    "asleep, hidden, exact and stays change how something works. Someone hidden goes out of sight once they get there. exact means they don't vary the time. stays means the same place on that level every day, as asleep does. every means only on every so many days.",
    "doing is what the player and the game master are told. Keep the secrets out of it, because what someone's doing can be seen, but not why.",
    "crowd is everyone without a file. Each group has a list of names, and shift moves that person's whole day later by that many minutes."
  ],
